WEBVTT

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:12.450
Aletta, tape.

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:13.490
Here.

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:19.540
Well, it's beginning to look 
quite festive in here.

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:21.560
Thank you!

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:26.670
Are you sure you want to start 
eating already, Artorius-san?

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:30.390
Yes, you'll have to pardon 
me for starting early.

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:32.920
The Day of Satur only comes 
once every seven days.

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:36.930
I want to take my time enjoying 
this to the fullest.

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:48.950
You really look forward to coming here, huh?

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:50.150
Indeed.

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:51.250
Okay...

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:54.370
What should I start preparing first?

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:58.470
Most of my customers order 
the same thing every time,

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:00.130
so I need to make a lot of it.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.520
Right, let's do this!

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:43.300
It hasn't changed at all.

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:03.110
Welcome!

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:06.450
<i>When did he hire part-time staff?</i>

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:08.700
<i>A young demon girl, and...</i>

00:03:09.190 --> 00:03:10.500
<i>Is that...</i>

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:14.940
<i>That fool. Of all the help 
he could have hired...</i>

00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:18.300
<i>Thankfully, she doesn't seem malicious,</i>

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:23.100
<i>but one wrong move, and she could destroy 
not only Nekoya, but the whole world.</i>

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:26.610
Um, is this your first time here?

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:29.140
No, I've been here before, long ago.

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:32.580
I see! I'll show you to your table, then.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:34.600
No need for that.

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:35.520
Huh?

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:41.780
Long time no see, Art.

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:45.280
Hm? Oh, if it isn't Yomi!

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:47.790
Do you mind if I sit with you?

00:03:48.190 --> 00:03:49.540
Of course not.

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:50.880
Thank you.

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:53.440
Yomi-san?

00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:58.050
Here's your wet hand towel 
and complimentary water.

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:00.620
And this is our menu.

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:02.120
Thank you.

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:06.370
S-Sure! If there's anything 
you need, just let me know!

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:07.550
Yes...

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:10.880
The menu has grown quite a bit.

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:14.580
I suppose that proves just 
how hard he's been working.

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:19.070
And you still order the pork 
loin cutlet with beer, I see.

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:27.240
They are the ultimate pairing, after all.

00:04:30.810 --> 00:04:36.100
The last time I saw you was when 
the previous master passed on.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:38.130
So, about ten years ago?

00:04:38.890 --> 00:04:42.530
That's right. It's really been 
that long since Daiki died.

00:04:43.130 --> 00:04:44.570
Daiki?

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:47.480
Excuse me. Another beer, please.

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:50.030
Oh... Coming right up!

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:56.480
Oh, by the way...

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:58.940
Is today a special occasion?

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:04.190
The Princess of the Empire and the Prince 
of the Land of Sand are getting married,

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:07.000
and the after-party is being held here.

00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:10.050
The Empire and the Land of Sand?

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:12.440
Well, that's quite a change.

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:17.170
Thank you for waiting. Here's your beer.

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:19.350
Thank you.

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:21.120
May I order?

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.170
Sure!

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:26.680
The pork loin cutlet with rice.
And extra rice, please.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:29.810
Coming right up! Please wait just a moment!

00:05:31.610 --> 00:05:35.430
Anyway, I'm surprised to see 
a demon working for him now.

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:40.940
Times have changed. 
They aren't our enemies anymore.

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:43.060
I know.

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:45.190
Still, it makes me remember...

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:52.950
the days we spent with swords in our hands,
 just slaying demons everywhere.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:59.180
Indeed... It's been 70 years 
since we traveled together.

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:03.680
But when that evil god sent 
you to the other world,

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:06.390
I thought there was no way you'd survived.

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:10.660
I thought I was a goner then, too.

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:11.550
But...

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:17.740
<i>Hey! Are you okay?</i>

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:21.690
Hey! Hey! Open your eyes!

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:23.130
Please open your eyes!

00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:48.470
Do you understand what I'm saying?

00:06:50.650 --> 00:06:51.920
Are you hurt?

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:52.970
I'm all right.

00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:56.470
Why were you in the ocean 
at this time of year?

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:59.980
You weren't actually 
trying to die, were you?

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:05.600
Are you hungry?

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:11.740
Okay! I just got some good 
meat in. I'll treat you.

00:07:13.130 --> 00:07:14.490
But...

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:16.010
Don't worry about it.

00:07:20.130 --> 00:07:23.620
My name's Yamagata Daiki. What's yours?

00:07:24.350 --> 00:07:27.360
Yomi. They call me Yomi.

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:48.840
<b>Western
Food
Stall</b>

00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:06.900
It seems you lived a good 
life in the other world.

00:08:09.530 --> 00:08:10.680
I did.

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:14.470
Thank you for waiting!

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:19.470
<i>Pork Loin Cutlet</i>

00:08:15.940 --> 00:08:18.460
Here's your pork loin 
cutlet with extra rice.

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:21.100
Thank you.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:22.510
Enjoy!

00:08:27.130 --> 00:08:28.660
Time to eat.

00:08:30.370 --> 00:08:34.000
<i>The first slice should always be eaten as-is.</i>

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:38.940
<i>The breading has that freshly-fried aroma,</i>

00:08:38.940 --> 00:08:42.240
<i>and the tender meat has 
been prepared with care.</i>

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:45.610
<i>The more I chew it, 
the sweeter the oil tastes.</i>

00:08:45.610 --> 00:08:46.940
Delicious.

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:50.000
Pork loin cutlet really is 
the ultimate dish, isn't it?

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:52.260
I agree.

00:08:52.870 --> 00:08:54.760
Now, next...

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:23.470
<i>Nothing beats Worcestershire 
sauce for pork loin cutlets!</i>

00:09:23.470 --> 00:09:25.340
<i>The sweet, salty flavor of the sauce,</i>

00:09:25.340 --> 00:09:27.680
<i>and the sour bite of the lemon...</i>

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:33.360
<i>And the spicy heat of the 
mustard fills my nose,</i>

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:37.260
<i>softening the richness of the oil so 
that I can keep eating more and more!</i>

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:39.820
<i>And the rice...</i>

00:09:39.820 --> 00:09:42.520
<i>There's no better match 
for pork loin cutlet.</i>

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:48.830
<i>Each individual grain is so glossy, 
and eating it at the same time</i>

00:09:48.830 --> 00:09:51.280
<i>brings out the savoriness of the cutlet.</i>

00:09:52.640 --> 00:09:57.360
<i>The cabbage is finely chopped, 
with a refreshing flavor.</i>

00:09:57.360 --> 00:10:01.600
<i>It cleanses my palate so I don't 
get tired of eating the cutlet.</i>

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:08.080
You eat that as if you truly enjoy it.

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:13.340
Oh, but if you like a dish, 
it's rude not to treat it as such.

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:15.260
That is true.

00:10:32.470 --> 00:10:35.300
<i>It's still no match for Daiki's cooking,</i>

00:10:35.300 --> 00:10:38.200
<i>but he certainly has improved.</i>

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:41.950
Pardon me. Could you call 
the master out here for me?

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:44.620
I have something to give him.

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:47.200
Of course.

00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:53.710
I thought so.

00:10:53.950 --> 00:10:56.460
The extra rice order was yours, Grandma.

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:59.590
If you knew it was me, 
you could have said something.

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:03.100
G-Grandma?!

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:06.020
Yeah. This is my grandma.

00:11:06.020 --> 00:11:09.110
What?! I had no idea!

00:11:09.110 --> 00:11:11.350
Well, you've never seen her before.

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:15.610
But I guess you do look... 
similar... sort of?

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:20.770
I think I look more like 
my grandpa, actually.

00:11:21.670 --> 00:11:23.120
You do indeed.

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:25.430
So what is it you have for me?

00:11:27.550 --> 00:11:28.380
Right...

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:31.620
It's this.

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:32.990
A key?

00:11:32.990 --> 00:11:35.630
The master key to the front door.

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:39.630
Master key? The one I have isn't the master?

00:11:40.020 --> 00:11:41.150
No.

00:11:41.150 --> 00:11:44.040
And this is not merely a key.

00:11:44.440 --> 00:11:49.020
It holds a power that is 
very special to Nekoya.

00:11:51.030 --> 00:11:54.020
The power to bring the Restaurant 
to Another World to an end.

00:11:55.020 --> 00:11:56.900
Bring the Restaurant to Another World...

00:11:56.900 --> 00:11:58.650
...to an end?

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:09.970
After Daiki died, I thought I would 
be the one to end this restaurant.

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:14.380
But you have done a fine job 
keeping the business going.

00:12:14.380 --> 00:12:19.870
So when the time comes that you feel ready 
to end the Restaurant to Another World,

00:12:19.870 --> 00:12:22.050
break this key.

00:12:23.650 --> 00:12:28.140
Once you do, the door will never 
again lead to the other world.

00:12:29.170 --> 00:12:30.330
I see...

00:12:31.180 --> 00:12:32.880
Master...

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:36.810
I won't end it.

00:12:37.140 --> 00:12:38.870
Grandpa said to me...

00:12:39.660 --> 00:12:43.950
If anything happens to me, 
I'm leaving everything to you.

00:12:44.690 --> 00:12:47.200
You can keep the restaurant 
going or shut it down.

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:51.200
But if you can, I hope you'll keep it going.

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:55.200
This place is special to me.

00:12:56.630 --> 00:12:58.280
That was Grandpa's request.

00:12:58.640 --> 00:13:00.790
So long as I'm healthy, 
I won't shut it down.

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:05.080
I see. Still, you should keep the key.

00:13:05.520 --> 00:13:06.200
Sure.

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:08.930
Thank goodness!

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:12.140
I thought I'd never get to 
eat chicken curry again.

00:13:12.420 --> 00:13:14.790
They're quite fond of you, aren't they?

00:13:17.350 --> 00:13:18.960
Well, until next time.

00:13:19.750 --> 00:13:22.340
I hope it'll be a wonderful party.

00:13:22.340 --> 00:13:23.100
Thanks.

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:25.530
Take care, Art.

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:28.280
Indeed. See you again.

00:13:29.640 --> 00:13:31.790
Thank you very much.

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:45.010
<i>Buffet</i>

00:13:49.730 --> 00:13:52.240
So many customers came to eat with us!

00:13:52.240 --> 00:13:52.890
Yes.

00:13:54.810 --> 00:13:56.980
Ah, the guests of honor have arrived!

00:13:56.980 --> 00:14:01.480
Congratulations!

00:14:03.330 --> 00:14:05.390
Congratulations on your wedding!

00:14:05.390 --> 00:14:06.360
Thank you.

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:08.040
Thank you so much!

00:14:09.560 --> 00:14:11.910
Thank you all for joining us today.

00:14:12.560 --> 00:14:14.540
We're so happy that we can 
celebrate this occasion

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:19.190
here at Nekoya, the place 
where the two of us met.

00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:23.340
The road to our wedding 
was long, and we first—

00:14:29.050 --> 00:14:33.230
I'm sorry, Brother. That was me.

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:36.960
We don't want the food to get cold.

00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:40.610
Let's keep the speeches 
short and enjoy our meal.

00:14:40.610 --> 00:14:42.900
Yeah, you're right.

00:14:43.290 --> 00:14:45.900
Now, in celebration of this day...

00:14:46.510 --> 00:14:47.650
Cheers!

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:49.360
Cheers!

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:54.760
A-Are these all pizzas?

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:56.630
Looks like it.

00:14:56.630 --> 00:14:57.930
I'll start with this one.

00:15:00.250 --> 00:15:03.050
<i>The mild tartness of the white sauce</i>

00:15:03.050 --> 00:15:06.320
<i>and the sweetness of the yellow 
vegetable fill my mouth!</i>

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:08.010
<i>It's so good!</i>

00:15:08.010 --> 00:15:12.580
<i>I've seen this yellow vegetable 
before in our world.</i>

00:15:13.160 --> 00:15:15.760
<i>The question is what this white sauce is.</i>

00:15:16.050 --> 00:15:17.930
<i>It's not knight's sauce...</i>

00:15:18.260 --> 00:15:20.400
<i>What is it made from?</i>

00:15:20.990 --> 00:15:23.150
<i>Jonathan had the white one, huh?</i>

00:15:23.990 --> 00:15:25.770
<i>I'll try the green one.</i>

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:30.410
<i>The fragrant herbs and 
perfect amount of salt...</i>

00:15:30.990 --> 00:15:33.600
<i>Does the sauce have powdered cheese in it?</i>

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:36.080
<i>The rich aroma lingers in my nose!</i>

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:39.620
Pizza is such a profound dish.

00:15:40.480 --> 00:15:42.830
Let's remember the flavor well 
and take it back with us.

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:43.670
Right!

00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:45.520
What is this?

00:15:45.520 --> 00:15:47.430
It smells good.

00:15:47.430 --> 00:15:49.890
Maybe you're supposed to put 
it on top of something?

00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:02.190
Yum!

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:03.570
Let me try.

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:07.340
It is good!

00:16:07.340 --> 00:16:09.440
Let's put it on some other things, too.

00:16:09.730 --> 00:16:12.130
Rice goes best with curry.

00:16:13.210 --> 00:16:15.070
Rice?

00:16:16.930 --> 00:16:18.220
It's delicious!

00:16:18.220 --> 00:16:19.820
I can't get enough of this!

00:16:19.820 --> 00:16:22.070
I could keep eating bowl after bowl!

00:16:24.360 --> 00:16:27.500
I bet this would be great with cheese on it!

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:29.590
That does sound delicious.

00:16:29.590 --> 00:16:31.450
We have cheese over here.

00:16:33.280 --> 00:16:35.880
It looks like it'd be amazing on its own!

00:16:35.880 --> 00:16:39.220
Yes, but it definitely 
seems worth testing out.

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:41.320
Okay, let's try it!

00:16:43.380 --> 00:16:46.610
Come to think of it, 
I don't see any pudding.

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:49.070
There's no fruit jelly, either.

00:16:49.070 --> 00:16:51.630
I was looking forward to eating some...

00:16:51.630 --> 00:16:54.970
Actually, I don't see any sweets at all.

00:16:54.970 --> 00:16:56.120
Everyone!

00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:57.740
Thank you for waiting!

00:16:57.740 --> 00:17:00.180
This is a gift from the master!

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:08.000
Congratulations on your wedding.
 Please enjoy this.

00:17:09.200 --> 00:17:10.500
It's so big!

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:10.500
Cake?

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:11.600
Thank you.

00:17:11.600 --> 00:17:13.510
Thank you so much!

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:15.260
Here, use this.

00:17:15.260 --> 00:17:16.760
What is that?!

00:17:16.760 --> 00:17:20.010
Oh, sorry. That's just in this world.

00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:24.880
It's traditional here for the new 
bride and groom to cut the cake.

00:17:25.260 --> 00:17:27.230
Oh... Well, then...

00:17:27.230 --> 00:17:28.210
Yes.

00:17:33.250 --> 00:17:34.250
Here goes.

00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:35.090
Yes.

00:17:42.760 --> 00:17:44.910
So... what happens now?

00:17:44.910 --> 00:17:48.060
Ah, I'll cut it up for serving.

00:17:48.590 --> 00:17:50.680
Kuro, could you bring the plates?

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:51.510
Yes.

00:17:52.240 --> 00:17:56.100
Thank you, god of demons, 
for this, my daily bread!

00:17:56.100 --> 00:17:57.330
I shall now partake!

00:17:59.040 --> 00:18:01.930
It's so sweet and delicious!

00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:05.310
Delicious!

00:18:05.720 --> 00:18:08.710
The tartness of fruit, 
the fluffiness of cake,

00:18:08.710 --> 00:18:11.310
and the milky flavor of fresh cream 
are brought together as one.

00:18:11.310 --> 00:18:15.320
It's light and refreshing, 
but with a definite sweetness.

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:17.200
My usual is always good,

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:20.820
but it's nice to try something 
different every now and then.

00:18:21.140 --> 00:18:24.830
Eating something sweet is 
making me want a soda.

00:18:25.050 --> 00:18:28.080
You're welcome to order 
any drinks or desserts.

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:29.380
Really?

00:18:29.380 --> 00:18:33.340
Then I want a melon soda 
float with soft serve!

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:36.150
I'd like a mocha chocolate parfait, please.

00:18:36.150 --> 00:18:38.560
Pudding a la mode for me.

00:18:38.560 --> 00:18:40.840
I'd like fruit jelly, please.

00:18:40.840 --> 00:18:44.060
I'll take all three types of cheesecake!

00:18:44.060 --> 00:18:47.230
I'll have two mont blancs... no, three!

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:48.230
Sure thing.

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:50.270
I'll make the soda float.

00:18:50.270 --> 00:18:52.330
I'll help with things, too.

00:18:52.330 --> 00:18:54.230
Great, thanks.

00:18:56.860 --> 00:18:59.610
Here, Sharry. Open wide.

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:06.130
That's so good!

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:06.600
They look so happy. I love it.

00:19:06.930 --> 00:19:09.080
M-Minced Meat Cutlet!

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:13.590
Uh, what?

00:19:14.090 --> 00:19:16.090
Could we also...

00:19:20.230 --> 00:19:22.590
be like the two of them?!

00:19:22.590 --> 00:19:24.100
What?

00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:27.100
Wait, where the heck did that come from?!

00:19:27.100 --> 00:19:29.380
I... I love you, Minced Meat Cutlet!

00:19:29.960 --> 00:19:31.100
Please marry me!

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:39.240
<i>Sarah-san and Heinrich-san 
might get married?!</i>

00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:43.240
<i>If they do that, I might not 
get to work for her anymore!</i>

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:45.660
W-Wait just a second!

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:47.620
A-Aletta?!

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:51.000
Sarah-san is mine!

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:53.080
What?!

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:54.330
What?!

00:19:54.330 --> 00:19:56.650
Wait, what does that even mean?!

00:19:56.650 --> 00:19:58.750
Ah, um...

00:19:58.750 --> 00:20:01.710
I want Sarah-san to be happy,

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:05.510
but I don't want to lose my job!

00:20:06.610 --> 00:20:10.740
Don't worry, Aletta. 
I don't intend to get married.

00:20:10.740 --> 00:20:11.420
Huh?

00:20:11.420 --> 00:20:12.230
Wha?!

00:20:12.230 --> 00:20:14.750
Talk about a bad rehash!

00:20:14.750 --> 00:20:17.360
You thought you could take advantage 
of the mood to propose?

00:20:17.690 --> 00:20:18.480
Hmph!

00:20:18.480 --> 00:20:21.930
N-No! I wasn't taking advantage of...

00:20:25.340 --> 00:20:29.020
I-It is true that the mood 
here inspired me, but...

00:20:32.350 --> 00:20:34.490
N-No... I'm sorry!

00:20:39.320 --> 00:20:40.760
Hey, there's always next time.

00:20:40.760 --> 00:20:42.850
Just go for the next one!

00:20:43.260 --> 00:20:45.010
N-Next one?!

00:21:33.780 --> 00:21:35.570
Everyone looks happy.

00:21:35.570 --> 00:21:38.020
Yes, they do.

00:21:38.020 --> 00:21:39.850
What's wrong? Tired?

00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:42.350
Ah, no, that's not it.

00:21:43.620 --> 00:21:46.840
Watching everyone today made 
me think about something.

00:21:46.840 --> 00:21:53.200
Delicious cooking transcends country 
and race to make people happy.

00:21:53.200 --> 00:21:58.500
Before I came to Nekoya, I had no 
idea cooking had that kind of power.

00:22:00.080 --> 00:22:03.090
Your cooking really is amazing, Master!

00:22:04.580 --> 00:22:09.050
I'm so happy I found that door,

00:22:09.050 --> 00:22:11.060
along with such a precious place!

00:22:11.060 --> 00:22:13.850
Me, too. I'm sure everyone 
feels the same way.

00:22:16.760 --> 00:22:18.190
Thanks.
